 operands without panicking during emit\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1422\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":390,\"title\":\"fix(services): reject self-referential shapes before resolving their types\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1423\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":391,\"title\":\"fix(modules): emit hygienic module holders and export properties\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1424\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":392,\"title\":\"fix(modules): assign CommonJS module re-exports\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1425\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":393,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): call plain defaults through every import shape\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1426\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":394,\"title\":\"fix(match): a class pattern's arm runs only for an instance of its class\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: cases match-class-patterns (runnable: same-named classes, `is`, a family base, a structural object, a refusing custom matcher, a structural object reaching an Option arm, and the check as a statement, in an expression and in an Effect function), match-class-patterns.fail (EK4701 for both look-alikes), match-exhaustive-coverage (V8 block coverage of every arm misses only a non-finite match's $noMatch), and match-exhaustive-last-arm's regenerated arms.js; a runtime test for $assertMatch.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1427\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":395,\"title\":\"chore(forms): regenerate the forms table and its decisions\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1428\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":396,\"title\":\"fix(handlers): a non-tail resume's type covers every value the handle can end with\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1429\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":397,\"title\":\"fix(errors): a family base's schema accepts its subclasses, and a subclass's _tag field must include its name\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: cases decl-schema-error-family and decl-error-family-own-tag.fail, runtime tests/schema-errors.test.ts. D304 amended; the expected-errors guide, the EK2117 row, token counts and generated pages updated.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1430\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":398,\"title\":\"fix(services): warn of the services an entry module's main needs\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: case entry-main-services.fail (a service needed directly, through a called function and beyond a provide block; a provided main, a main with a parameter, an unexported main, imported, namespaced and re-exported mains, type-only and side-effect importers; a module that runs main itself) and entry-main-services-error.fail (the error setting).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1431\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":399,\"title\":\"fix(checker): a typed const holds its initializer through as, satisfies and !\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1432\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":400,\"title\":\"fix(checker): a typed const holds both branches of a conditional initializer\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1433\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":401,\"title\":\"fix(checker): a typed const holds a pipe initializer\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1434\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":402,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): a pipe in an Effect-typed field keeps its function plain for callers\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1435\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":403,\"title\":\"fix(forms): a lambda's own type says nothing about its form\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: case lambda-own-contextual-type (runnable: a one- and a two-parameter generic check of a lambda that returns an Effect subtype; TS7024 on both calls before). Docs: a dated note on D44.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1436\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":404,\"title\":\"fix(forms): an annotated lambda may call the variable it initializes\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: case annotated-lambda-reads-its-variable (runnable; TS7022 before).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1437\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":405,\"title\":\"fix(forms): a factory lambda that returns an Effect keeps TypeScript's type\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: case factory-lambda-infers-channels (runnable, with a type-level check that the call needs nothing; TS2344 and EK2002 before). Docs: a dated note on D269.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1438\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":406,\"title\":\"fix(provide): a generic requirement keeps Exclude<R, I> of a provide block\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: case provide-generic-requirement (runnable, with a type-level check that the call needs nothing; TS2344 and EK2002 before). Docs: a dated note on D173.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1439\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":407,\"title\":\"fix(declarations): a .vibe file's header comment stays first in its declaration file\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1440\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":408,\"title\":\"fix(declarations): a function expression's written contract is its declaration's type\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1441\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":409,\"title\":\"fix(checker): a restore block inside an uninterruptible expression is inside one\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1442\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":410,\"title\":\"fix(parser): a schema declaration keeps its comments where they were written\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1443\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":411,\"title\":\"fix(lowering): a name the lowering adds never repeats a module declaration's import\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: cases module-declaration-generated-names (the runtime and effect/Effect), module-import-generated-names (effect/Effect alone) and module-declaration-import-names (a data method's effect/Option import).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1444\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":412,\"title\":\"fix(diagnostics): a diagnostics comment can give its reason after punctuation\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1445\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":413,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): CommonJS output calls an imported plain function's plain variant\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: the acceptance case plain-import-shapes-cjs, loaded with require like module-declaration-cjs, covers every shape of plain-default-import- shapes plus named, renamed and string-named imports, a tagged template, a function value passed to map, a call from Effect code, and an export list before its import.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1446\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":414,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): `export default f` of a plain function exports its plain variant\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: the acceptance cases plain-export-default-assign (ES module) and plain-export-default-assign-cjs (CommonJS, loaded with require) cover a local function, an imported one, a renamed import, a namespace member, a default re-exported with `export { default } from`, and a function value.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1447\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":415,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): a direct async hatch gives its function exactly its inputs, and the signal only where its overload passes one\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: the acceptance case hatches-direct-params (rest parameters typed number and unknown, sync and try with and without a mapper, an optional and a defaulted parameter, a function taking the signal, inline arrows, and interruption aborting the signal) failed before with rest 3 and optional \\\"object\\\"; a runtime test of $asyncHatch.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1448\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":416,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): a throw that can escape a constructor, an accessor, a static block or the top level is a compile error\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1449\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":417,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): super and arguments work in Effect methods, Effect arrows and try regions\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1450\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":418,\"title\":\"fix(forms): a lambda for an optional member takes the member's contract\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1451\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":419,\"title\":\"fix(diagnostics): a contract suggestion keeps a never success\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Test: TestBangTypes (bang_test.go).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1452\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":420,\"title\":\"fix(returns): a returned pipe that ends in a call returns what the call returns\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1453\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":421,\"title\":\"fix(lower): a by-name program never prints its expression's leading comments after its return\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1454\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":422,\"title\":\"fix(checker): a for...of over a Stream adds its failures and requirements with their source\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1455\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":423,\"title\":\"fix(forms): a factory lambda in a branch of a conditional argument keeps the type TypeScript infers\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1456\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":424,\"title\":\"fix(parser): a function literal on a pipe left side stays a program for a curried stage\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1457\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":425,\"title\":\"fix(hatches): a destructuring property name inside a hatch is no capture\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1458\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":426,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): an optional call of a callback without a contract runs it\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1459\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":427,\"title\":\"fix(diagnostics): EK4802 reports an Effect value in a returned conditional's arm\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1460\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":428,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): a file whose functions only throw or produce loads effect\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1461\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":429,\"title\":\"fix(diagnostics): warn where a program's value is a call of an any-typed value\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1462\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":430,\"title\":\"fix(diagnostics): EK4802 reports an Effect value returned where the success names no value\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1463\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":431,\"title\":\"test(returns): a returned pipe keeps an Exit under a mask, in two stages and under a written success\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1464\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":432,\"title\":\"fix(recursion): a function that passes a call of itself by name gets EK2102, not a stack overflow\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1465\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":433,\"title\":\"fix(lower): a lowered return keeps a commented value on its line\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1466\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":434,\"title\":\"fix(lower): an uninterruptible block that owns a using resource stays uninterruptible\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1467\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":435,\"title\":\"fix(printer): a comment the compiler moves after return, throw or yield stays a comment\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: case keyword-operand-comments (each form with a line comment and a block comment, run under node: on 0.0.5 it dies with \\\"Not a valid effect: undefined\\\", and its JavaScript has 13 returns followed by a line break); printer tests TestParenthesizeMovedExpressionForNoAsi, TestPartiallyEmittedExpressionCommentOnLaterLine and TestTokenCommentsOnlyWhereTheSourceHoldsTheToken.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1468\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":436,\"title\":\"fix(diagnostics): EK4802 reports a program returned by name where the success names no value\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1469\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":437,\"title\":\"fix(diagnostics): EK4802 reports a returned union that can be a program where the success names no value\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1470\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":438,\"title\":\"fix(diagnostics): EK2004 warns where a plain catch lets a TypeScript call's exception through\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1471\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":439,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): a file whose functions only parse JSON or decode URIs loads effect\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1472\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":440,\"title\":\"fix(diagnostics): EK1012 warns where a stored call never succeeds\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1473\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":441,\"title\":\"docs(compiler): identify the TypeScript fork and route project guidance\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1474\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":442,\"title\":\"docs(resources): explain pending interruption disposal window\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1475\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":443,\"title\":\"docs(language): match contract and interoperability claims to the compiler\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1476\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":444,\"title\":\"docs(effect): replace application internals with general examples\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1477\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":445,\"title\":\"docs(trust): teach the current runtime wrapper\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1478\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":446,\"title\":\"docs(effect): explain the exact pin and cleanup incompatibility\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1479\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":447,\"title\":\"docs(services): say the starter sets EK3205 to an error\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1480\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":448,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): a handle clause tail resume in a for concurrent body is not EK4606\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1481\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":449,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): EK4201 reports control operations that fork, the await operations and for concurrent run on another fiber\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1482\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":450,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): a comma between the fields of an error, service or control is EK1013\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: the case error-field-commas.fail pins EK1013 for each body kind (on main each is TS1442); TestEditorQuickFixGoldens applies the fix for an error, a schema error and a service. Chapter 28's code table, the compiler README and the expected-errors guide document the code.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1483\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":451,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): a hover on a by-name argument no longer leaves its call inferred as unknown\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Test: TestEditorHoverOnByNameArgumentBeforeCheck hovers the first topic and then the second; on main the second is unknown.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1484\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":452,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): EK4401 suggests a try call that compiles and the trusted() wrapper\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: TestEK4401SuggestionCompiles compiles each suggestion in place of the call; on main three of its five suggestions differ and do not compile. The cases ek4401-boundary-operands.fail and ek4401-effect-reexports.fail pin the new notes.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1485\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":453,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): CommonJS output binds the names a file takes from the prelude\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Test: the case prelude-imports-cjs, the starter's sources plus sleep, flow and pipe in a CommonJS package, prints its three lines; on main it throws.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1486\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":454,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): EK3201 says a program of type any has unknown services instead of naming any\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Test: the case ek3201-any-program.fail; on main its messages.txt is not printed (\\\"no provider for any.\\\").\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1487\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":455,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): EK2003's hatch note says what try makes of the exception\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Test: the case plain-throw-escapes.fail's messages.txt holds the new line; on main it is missing. The expected-errors guide shows the same output.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1488\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":456,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): \\\"Did you mean\\\" offers the prelude's names in a .vibe file\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Test: the case prelude-spelling.fail (Consle -> Console, sleeep -> sleep, Mat -> Math); on main the first suggests console and the second nothing.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1489\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":457,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): hold a Layer.effect block's members to the service's contract\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1490\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":458,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): don't crash on grammar errors in jumps, loops and Effect forms\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1491\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":459,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): type a self-call by its contract's A while the fixpoint runs\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1492\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":460,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): close a for...of loop's iterator when its body fails\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1493\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":461,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): name the code that cannot run a program, and fit EK4301's fix\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1494\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":462,\"title\":\"fix(ts-mapper): keep the stock TypeScript pin in one place\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1495\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":463,\"title\":\"fix(ts-mapper): run the stock-compiler tests in e2e instead of skipping them\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1496\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":464,\"title\":\"fix(ts-mapper): test against TypeScript 7.1 Beta\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1497\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":465,\"title\":\"fix(ts-mapper): a new mapper build invalidates tsc --build outputs\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1498\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":466,\"title\":\"docs(ts-mapper): say the TypeScript 7.1 content mapper is experimental and unpublished\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1499\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":467,\"title\":\"feat(compiler): data declarations lower to Effect's Data.TaggedEnum and match by variant\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: cases data-declaration (runs and prints; pins main.d.ts), data-import (a recursive generic type across files; pins shapes.d.ts), data-ts-consumer (TypeScript constructs, narrows and $matches through the declaration file), data-match-emit (pins the emitted guard and the untested last arm), data-declaration.fail and data-patterns.fail (each code, with messages); TestEditorQuickFixGoldens (EK1013 for a data variant and its fields); TestDataDeclarationIsAClassOfItsVariants.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1500\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":468,\"title\":\"feat(mapper): say the TypeScript 7 mapper does not lower data declarations\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Test: TestDataDeclarationIsUnprojected (two declarations, one plain and one generic: one EK9001 each, at the declaration, and a valid map).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1501\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":469,\"title\":\"feat(compiler)!: EK1014 retires the ! form; Effect<A> means Effect<A, never, never>\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1502\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":470,\"title\":\"fix(fix): write only the project's own files, not a dependency's source\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1503\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":471,\"title\":\"fix(fix): halve a refused round instead of checking once per file; stop cleanly on SIGTERM\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1504\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":472,\"title\":\"fix(declarations): import the prelude names of typeof queries and copied library types\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1505\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":473,\"title\":\"feat(compiler): the ! form compiles again beside Effect<...>; retire EK1014\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1506\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":474,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): resolve relative project import paths\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1507\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":475,\"title\":\"fix(parser): explain redundant do before direct blocks\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1508\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":476,\"title\":\"fix(match): capture the subject before entering arm scopes\",\"s