s\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1629\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":597,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): preserve comments across source rewrites\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1630\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":598,\"title\":\"test(checker): more provider cases\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1631\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":599,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): fail with a throw's operand, and reject a throw of a Cause\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Landed by the merge queue from lane implx through mq-10280258-1 (matched by title).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1632\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":600,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): declarations import Effect's modules from effect\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1633\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":601,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): Readonly's object type declares no readonly of its own\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1634\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":602,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): inferred declarations name effect modules as the source does\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1635\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":603,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): test an exhaustive match's last arm, and match functions with object patterns\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1636\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":604,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): keep both failures when a for...of closes its iterator\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1637\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":605,\"title\":\"fix(parser): parse a parenthesized await operation as a call\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1638\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":606,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): report a control operation's Stream at every consumer\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1639\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":607,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): recurse on heap frames in plain-annotated call cycles\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Landed by the merge queue from lane implx through mq-10280358-1 (matched by title).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1640\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":608,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): a ! form's empty trailing slots stay out of its declaration\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1641\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":609,\"title\":\"chore(forms): record the declaration identity cases' form decisions\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1642\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":610,\"title\":\"feat(checker): a service's identifier is nominal, and its brand is required (D361)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Before: the brand was optional, so a structural type such as Effect<number, never, { value: number }> was assignable to a requirement of either of two services with that member.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"},{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"After: that program is a compile error (EK2002 where the contract closes R, TS2322 where the requirement is assigned to B's).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"},{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Before: Users.Shape did not exist in the declarations.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1643\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":611,\"title\":\"feat(checker): error classes are nominal, and only closed classes count for coverage (D407)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Before: a match over classes a .ts file declares, over a TypeScript-style class in a .vibe file, over Error, or over a class with its own [Symbol.hasInstance] or [customMatcher] was proven exhaustive, and a value of the class's type that failed the instanceof test died at the last arm; a same-shaped class from another module was assignable to an error declaration.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1644\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":612,\"title\":\"feat(checker): a compiled error declaration carries its error marker (D407)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Before: an unmarked declaration-file class with an error's shape, and any class of effect with a literal _tag, such as cluster's IncomingEnvelope, counted toward a match's exhaustiveness. After: they are open (EK4701).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1645\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":613,\"title\":\"feat(compiler): a block param is always its call's last argument (S2)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Before: a block after an Effect dual took the place of its program.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"},{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"After: `f(args) { body }` is `f(args, () => { body })` and `f { body }` is `f(() => { body })`, whatever `f` is (D376).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1646\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":614,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): compile each module declaration to a JavaScript module of its own\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Landed by the merge queue from lane d403 through mq-10280816-3 (matched by title).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1647\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":615,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): a declaration's names join the import of effect a file keeps\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1648\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":616,\"title\":\"test(compiler): a Context.Service class kept in .vibe declares what its TypeScript did\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Landed by the merge queue from lane decl through mq-10280816-3 (matched by title).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1649\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":617,\"title\":\"feat(compiler): a fiber belongs to its named region, and an escaping one is EK4838 (D408, D409)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Before: a fork belonged to the innermost block, so an if branch, a bare block or a do block interrupted its fiber at its closing brace, and an arrow's expression body had no owner: `() => fork p()` was Effect.forkScoped with Scope in R (D96).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1650\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":618,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): a getter that returns an owned fiber is EK4838 (D409)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1651\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":619,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): enforce EK1019 inside do expressions\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Landed by the merge queue from lane ek1019 through mq-10281123-3 (matched by title).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1652\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":620,\"title\":\"chore(forms): record S2 block placement at service-identity\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1653\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":621,\"title\":\"feat(compiler): vibelang --fix writes Effect.gen in direct style (D470)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: TestEffectGenQuickFixes, TestEffectGenRefusals, TestEffectGenFixRounds, TestMigrationCasesFix with migrate-effect-gen (TypeScript, runnable, its declarations) and migrate-effect-gen-fixed (what --fix writes, same result).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1654\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":622,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): an arm that only binds handles every case (D471)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: match-binding-exhaustive (runnable: literals, a binding alone, tags) fails on main with EK4701 and passes; match-binding-guard.fail keeps EK4701.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1655\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":623,\"title\":\"feat(compiler): EK4839 writes Effect's Match chains as match (D472)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: TestMatchChainQuickFixes, TestMatchChainRefusals, TestMatchChainNotReported, and tsforms-match with tsforms-match-fixed, which run with one result and emit the same declarations.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1656\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":624,\"title\":\"feat(compiler): EK4840 writes Option pipelines with Option's methods (D473)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: TestOptionPipeQuickFixes, TestOptionPipeRefusals, TestOptionPipeNotReported, and tsforms-option with tsforms-option-fixed, which run with one result and emit the same declarations. lsrules-style.fail's golden gains the two EK4840 warnings its pipe of a pipe now draws, and the legacy-site oracle is regenerated at the stack's tip.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1657\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":625,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): --fix drops several names of one import in one edit\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: TestOptionPipeQuickFixes's \\\"two names of one import\\\" and \\\"two names of a list on lines\\\" fail before (overlapping editor edits) and pass.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1658\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":626,\"title\":\"test(compiler): the Match and Option twins keep a site each rule refuses\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Landed by the merge queue from lane codemod through mq-10281123-3 (matched by title).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1659\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":627,\"title\":\"fix(checker): a match over an open subject needs default (D428, D346)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Landed by the merge queue from lane match-open through mq-10281141-4 (matched by title).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"},{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Before: EK4701 ran only for a finite union.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"},{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"After: checkExhaustive also checks an open subject: string or number without a literal type, unknown, any, object, an array, a type parameter, or a class that is not closed.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1660\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":628,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): deduplicate inferred effect channels\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"tried\",\"text\":\"Rejected in the merge queue (inferdedupe): conflicts with main in sqxtlykn: s that leave a `do` expression now report `EK1019`.', '']), (0, 0, ['- Repeated calls along a chain of functions without written contracts could make the compiler run out of memory.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"},{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Landed by the merge queue from lane inferdedupe through mq-1028-1822 (pushed by hand after the pusher's tracking fix) (matched by title).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m1661\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":629,\"title\":\"feat(compiler): EK4841 writes a schema constant after its type alias as a schema alias (D474)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1662\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":630,\"title\":\"feat(compiler): EK4842 imports Effect's Array and its siblings under other names (D475)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1663\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":631,\"title\":\"fix(compiler): EK4831's service keeps the declaration's indentation\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m1664\",\"epic\":\"e4\",\"rank\":632,\"