nded\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2974\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":6,\"title\":\"runtime: test trusted exceptions with instanceof\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2975\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":7,\"title\":\"runtime: register a Disposable's release with interruption masked\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2976\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":8,\"title\":\"runtime: keep the errors and inputs of a layer that provides nothing\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2977\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":9,\"title\":\"runtime: type continuations as Continuation<V, E, H>\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2978\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":10,\"title\":\"runtime: make a producer a Stream with a zero-capacity handoff\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2979\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":11,\"title\":\"runtime: add $isRun, $direct, and the fast-call protocol for the projector's JavaScript\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2980\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":12,\"title\":\"test(runtime): cover fiber collections, races, ownership, and bounded loops\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2981\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":13,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): cancel held await fibers on every exit (found by cancellation tests)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2982\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":14,\"title\":\"test(runtime): cover hatch failures, callback cancellation, and lazy execution\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2983\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":15,\"title\":\"test(runtime): cover providers, resource ownership, causes, and interruption masks\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2984\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":16,\"title\":\"test(runtime): exercise producer cleanup, completion records, and stack safety\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2985\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":17,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): register main signal handlers before observing completion (found by listener test)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2986\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":18,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): preserve proto data keys in pattern rest (found by destructuring property test)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2987\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":19,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): close delegated iterators on failure and abandonment (found by cleanup tests)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2988\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":20,\"title\":\"test(runtime): record async hatch signal gap and exact synchronous inputs\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2989\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":21,\"title\":\"test(runtime): cover upstream stream failures and suspended fast-call protocols\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2990\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":22,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): coerce numeric pattern rest keys (found by native destructuring test)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2991\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":23,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): invoke iterator methods without bind or call properties\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2992\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":24,\"title\":\"chore(runtime): refresh forms input digest after iterator fix\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2993\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":25,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): await callback interrupt finalizers (S19-30)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2994\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":26,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): using awaits Symbol.asyncDispose of a value nothing else releases\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: runtime tests for an awaited Symbol.asyncDispose on success, failure and interruption, in reverse order, a rejection as a defect, and a guard that a resource releasing itself keeps only its own release (Symbol.dispose still runs for it, per D94); acceptance cases scopes-using-async-dispose (the AsyncDisposable reproduction plus an acquireRelease) and scopes-using-pending-interrupt (pending: the interruption reproduction).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m2995\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":27,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): sync and try called as values pass an async function its AbortSignal\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: the two skipped runtime tests run and pass (sync and try give an async function the signal after its inputs); new runtime tests that interruption aborts that signal for both, that an async function with a rest or defaulted parameter, or none, gets exactly its inputs, and that a non-async function and an async generator function get no signal; the acceptance case hatches-value-signal (the reproduction, an input, the runtime's try imported under another name, rest and defaulted parameters, and a timeout that aborts the signal).\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m2996\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":28,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): dispose callable resources\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2997\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":29,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): accept callable iterables in await operations\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m2998\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":30,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): give defects precedence where the kernel combines causes\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: kernel laws K16a-K16d (K16a, K16b and K16d fail on the previous commit; K16c guards an expected cleanup failure). Runtime tests cover $catch, $catchExpression and $failureOf on a hand-built mixed cause.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m2999\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":31,\"title\":\"fix(runtime): catch recovers a failure beside an interruption, as Effect.catch does\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[{\"section\":\"evidence\",\"text\":\"Tests: K14c now asserts recovery of the first failure (it fails on the previous commit). K14d guards abandonment. A runtime catch-expression case covers Fail + Interrupt. The failures-mixed-causes row r6_interruptThenFinallyThrows now recovers in catch, catchMatch and catchValue.\",\"by\":\"bootstrap\"}]},{\"id\":\"m3000\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":32,\"title\":\"feat(runtime): Experimental.FileSystem and Experimental.Crypto (D313)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m3001\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":33,\"title\":\"feat(runtime): add Experimental.Process (D313)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m3002\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":34,\"title\":\"feat(runtime): add Experimental.Locks (D313)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m3003\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":35,\"title\":\"docs(runtime): complete the root export reference\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m3004\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":36,\"title\":\"feat(platform): Node.js reaches .vibe only through services or TypeScript (D310)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m3005\",\"epic\":\"e5\",\"rank\":37,\"title\":\"docs(platform): every platform global's example compiles on its page (D310)\",\"state\":\"landed\",\"task\":\"\",\"lane\":\"\",\"notes\":[]},{\"id\":\"m3006\",\"epic\":\